DTSTAMP:20251104T055848Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260101
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260102
SUMMARY:New Year's Day
DESCRIPTION:History: The Roman calendar fixed the turn of the civil year to
  January 1 under Julius Caesar\, and the Gregorian reform of 1582 reaffirm
 ed the date for much of the world.\nTraditions: Communities ring bells\, c
 ount down in packed squares\, exchange resolutions\, and watch fireworks o
 r televised celebrations to welcome a clean slate.\nFeasting: Families toa
 st with sparkling wine\, share longevity noodles or Hoppin' John for luck\
 , and slice sweet breads like panettone or king cakes to invite prosperity
 .\nDay: Thursday\n\nIcon: 🎊\nCategory: celebration\n\nAgenda: https://m
 ss.castalia.institute/agenda/new-years-day/\nRecipes:\nKir Royale: https:/
 /mss.castalia.institute/recipes/sparkling-wine/\nLongevity Noodles with Po
 rk and Vegetables: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/longevity-noodle
 s/\nHoppin' John: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/hoppin-john/\nTra
 ditional Panettone: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/panettone/\nTra
 ditional King Cake: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/king-cake/
CATEGORIES:celebration
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/new-years-day-champagne-and-confetti.png
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/new-years-day/
END:VEVENT
