SUMMARY:Perchta Day (Perchtenlauf)
DESCRIPTION:History: Alpine folklore honors Frau Perchta\, a wintry guardia
 n of hearth and spinning who inspected homes during the Twelve Nights afte
 r Christmas.\nTraditions: Villages in Austria and Bavaria host Perchtenlae
 ufe where masked figures parade with cowbells and torches to chase away da
 rkness and protect the fields.\nFeasting: Hosts offer dumplings\, poppy-se
 ed pastries\, and milky punches to the performers\, along with mulled wine
  and sweet krapfen for the crowd.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🎭\nCategory: cu
 ltural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/perchta-day-percht
 enlauf/\nRecipes:\nChinese Pork and Cabbage Dumplings (Jiaozi): https://ms
 s.castalia.institute/recipes/dumplings/\nPoppy Seed Pastries: https://mss.
 castalia.institute/recipes/poppy-seed-pastries/\nWarming Milky Punch: http
 s://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/milky-punch/\nTraditional Mulled Wine (
 Glühwein): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/mulled-wine/\nTradition
 al Austrian Krapfen: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/krapfen/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/austrian-and-bavarian-tradition-perchta-day.png
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/perchta-day-perchtenlauf/
END:VEVENT
