SUMMARY:Berchtoldstag
DESCRIPTION:History: Medieval Swiss guilds observed Berchtoldstag as a post
 -feast day to honor community bonds and start the civic year together.\nTr
 aditions: Families make Berchteln visits\, children knock on doors during 
 Baerzelistag parades\, and neighbors share well wishes with carved masks o
 r pine boughs.\nFeasting: Tables feature braided Zopf loaves\, roesti skil
 lets\, sausages\, hazelnut tortes\, and pots of melted cheese for communal
  dipping.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🍞\nCategory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https:
 //mss.castalia.institute/agenda/berchtoldstag/\nRecipes:\nZopf: https://ms
 s.castalia.institute/recipes/zopf/\nTraditional Rösti for Berchtoldstag: 
 https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/rosti/\nPan-Fried Swiss Cervelat wi
 th Onions: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/sausage/\nBerchtoldstag 
 Hazelnut Torte: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/hazelnut-torte/\nTr
 aditional Swiss Cheese Fondue: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/fond
 ue/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/berchtoldstag/
