DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260202
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260203
SUMMARY:Candlemas (Feast of the Presentation)
DESCRIPTION:History: Commemorated in Jerusalem by the fourth century\, Cand
 lemas marks forty days after Christmas when Mary and Joseph presented Jesu
 s at the Temple according to Mosaic law.\nTraditions: Churches bless candl
 es for the coming year\, processions illuminate winter nights\, and weathe
 r lore predicts the remaining length of winter.\nFeasting: La Chandeleur t
 ables offer crepes beurre sucre\, crepes jambon-fromage\, boles de cidre b
 rut\, and salade de mache\; in Mexico\, familias sirven tamales oaxaquenos
 \, tamales de dulce\, atole de canela\, champurrado espumoso\, and pan de 
 candelaria after the blessing of candles.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🕯️\nC
 ategory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/candlem
 as-feast-of-the-presentation/\nRecipes:\nCandlemas Crêpes with Butter and
  Sugar: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/crepes-with-butter-and-suga
 r/\nHam and Cheese Crepes for Candlemas: https://mss.castalia.institute/re
 cipes/ham-and-cheese-crepes/\nMulled Dry Cider for Candlemas: https://mss.
 castalia.institute/recipes/dry-cider/\nLamb's Lettuce Salad: https://mss.c
 astalia.institute/recipes/lambs-lettuce-salad/\nOaxacan Tamales: https://m
 ss.castalia.institute/recipes/oaxacan-tamales/\nSweet Tamales for Candlema
 s: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/sweet-tamales/\nCinnamon Atole: 
 https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/cinnamon-atole/\nFoamy Champurrado:
  https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/foamy-champurrado/\nCandlemas Brea
 d: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/candlemas-bread/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/candlemas-feast-of-the-presentation-of-jesus-and-blessing-of-candles.png
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/candlemas-feast-of-the-presentation/
