SUMMARY:Twelfth Night
DESCRIPTION:History: Twelfth Night concludes the Christmastide counting fro
 m medieval Europe\, blending Christian Epiphany vigils with older winter r
 evels.\nTraditions: Hosts crown a king or queen with hidden bean charms\, 
 wassailers sing at doorways\, and revelers dismantle greenery to avoid a y
 ear of bad fortune.\nFeasting: Tables feature spiced ale\, figgy puddings\
 , king cakes filled with almonds\, and roasted meats shared before the fas
 ting of Epiphany begins.\nDay: Monday\n\nIcon: 🎭\nCategory: cultural\n\
 nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/twelfth-night/\nRecipes:\nS
 piced Ale (Wassail): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/spiced-ale/\nF
 iggy Pudding: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/figgy-pudding/\nTradi
 tional King Cake: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/king-cake/\nRoast
 ed Pork Loin with Apple and Sage: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/r
 oasted-meat/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/twelfth-night-end-of-the-christmas-season.png
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/twelfth-night/
