SUMMARY:Epiphany (Three Kings Day)
DESCRIPTION:History: Since the second century\, Epiphany has celebrated the
  Magi recognising the Christ child\, symbolising the revelation of the div
 ine to the nations.\nTraditions: Families bless doorways with chalk\, stag
 e pageants of camels and kings\, and children receive gifts left by los Re
 yes Magos or La Befana.\nFeasting: Bakers craft rosca de reyes\, galette d
 es rois\, or king cakes\, while households sip rich hot chocolate and shar
 e slow-simmered stews.\nDay: Tuesday\n\nIcon: 👑\nCategory: cultural\n\n
 Agenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/epiphany-three-kings-day/\nR
 ecipes:\nRosca de Reyes (Three Kings' Bread): https://mss.castalia.institu
 te/recipes/rosca-de-reyes/\nGalette des Rois: https://mss.castalia.institu
 te/recipes/galette-des-rois/\nTraditional King Cake: https://mss.castalia.
 institute/recipes/king-cake/\nTraditional Holiday Hot Chocolate: https://m
 ss.castalia.institute/recipes/hot-chocolate/\nEpiphany Winter Beef Stew: h
 ttps://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/stew/
CATEGORIES:cultural
