SUMMARY:Fete de Papa Zaka - Feast of the Farmer Loa
DESCRIPTION:History: Haitian Vodou communities honour Papa Zaka, the kindly
  farmer lwa, during January gatherings to thank him for guarding crops and
  labouring families.\nTraditions: Altars are dressed with straw hats, ears
  of corn, bowls of grain, rum, and pipe tobacco while drummers, singers, a
 nd vodouisants petition Zaka for fertile fields before sharing food with n
 eighbours.\nFeasting: Aperitifs pour clairin ti punch, kleren anisette, an
 d pumpkin-spice jus giraumon; first courses carry soup joumou, accra de mo
 rue with pikliz, and mayi moulen ak sos pwa; mains feature poulet nan sos,
  griot de porc, legim nan diri, and red beans with rice; sides bring banna
 nn peze, pain mayi, and jars of pikliz; desserts finish with pen patat, bo
 nbons sirop, tropical fruits, and altar offerings of roasted corn, a grain
 -filled straw hat, and a shot of rum with pipe tobacco.\nDay: Saturday\n\n
 Icon: 🌾\nCategory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/a
 genda/fete-de-papa-zaka-feast-of-the-farmer-loa/\nRecipes:\nClairin Ti Pun
 ch: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/clairin-ti-punch/\nKleren Anise
 tte (Anise-Infused Clairin): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/kleren
 -anisette/\nPumpkin-Spice Jus Giraumon: https://mss.castalia.institute/rec
 ipes/pumpkin-spice-jus-giraumon/\nSoup Joumou: https://mss.castalia.instit
 ute/recipes/soup-joumou/\nAccra de Morue with Pikliz: https://mss.castalia
 .institute/recipes/accra-de-morue-with-pikliz/\nMayi Moulen ak Sos Pwa (Co
 rnmeal with Bean Sauce): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/mayi-moule
 n-ak-sos-pwa/\nPoulet Nan Sos (Haitian Chicken in Sauce): https://mss.cast
 alia.institute/recipes/poulet-nan-sos/\nGriot de Porc: https://mss.castali
 a.institute/recipes/griot-de-porc/\nLegim Nan Diri (Haitian Vegetable Stew
  with Rice): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/legim-nan-diri/\nRed B
 eans with Rice (Riz Collé ak Pwa Wouj): https://mss.castalia.institute/re
 cipes/red-beans-with-rice/\nBannann Peze (Twice-Fried Plantains): https://
 mss.castalia.institute/recipes/bannann-peze/\nPain Mayi (Haitian Corn Brea
 d): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/pain-mayi/\nPikliz: https://mss
 .castalia.institute/recipes/pikliz/\nPen Patat: https://mss.castalia.insti
 tute/recipes/pen-patat/\nBonbons Sirop (Haitian Lime Syrup Candies): https
 ://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/bonbons-sirop/\nPapa Zaka's Harvest Frui
 t Medley: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/tropical-fruits/\nRoasted
  Corn for Papa Zaka: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/roasted-corn/\
 nPapa Zaka's Spiced Rum Offering: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/r
 um/
