UID:old-twelfth-night-wassail@maybesomethingseasonal.com
DTSTAMP:20251104T055848Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260117
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260118
SUMMARY:Old Twelfth Night Wassail
DESCRIPTION:History: When Britain adopted the Gregorian calendar in 1752\, 
 many West Country farmers kept the old January date for Twelfth Night to b
 less orchards against blight.\nTraditions: Wassailers bang pans\, fire mus
 kets into branches\, and sing to wake the apple trees while offering cider
 -soaked toast to the guardian robin.\nFeasting: Hot mulled cider\, apple c
 akes\, blue cheese\, and pork pies fuel the rounds from farm to farm throu
 gh the frosty fields.\nDay: Saturday\n\nIcon: 🌟\nCategory: cultural\n\n
 Agenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/old-twelfth-night-wassail/\n
 Recipes:\nHot Mulled Cider for Wassail: https://mss.castalia.institute/rec
 ipes/hot-mulled-cider/\nTraditional Wassail Apple Cakes: https://mss.casta
 lia.institute/recipes/apple-cakes/\nBlue Cheese and Walnut Tart: https://m
 ss.castalia.institute/recipes/blue-cheese/\nHearty Pork Pies for Old Twelf
 th Night Wassail: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/pork-pies/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/old-twelfth-night-traditional-date-before-calendar-reform.png
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/old-twelfth-night-wassail/
