UID:feast-of-st-muirgen-li-ban-the-mermaid@maybesomethingseasonal.com
DTSTAMP:20260911T170000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260127
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260128
SUMMARY:Feast of St. Muirgen (Lí Ban the Mermaid)
DESCRIPTION:History: Lí Ban\, daughter of Eochaid\, survived the bursting 
 of Lough Neagh in a chamber beneath the waves and\, after a year\, was tra
 nsformed into a mermaid\, half woman and half salmon\, with her lapdog as 
 an otter. She swam the seas for three centuries until fishermen of St. Com
 gall of Bangor netted her at Larne Lough\; baptised Muirgen ("sea-born")\,
  she chose heaven at once and is venerated on 27 January.\nTraditions: Rea
 d her tale from the Annals of the Four Masters\, walk the shores of Lough 
 Neagh or Larne Lough\, and light a candle for sailors and all who live by 
 the sea.\nFeasting: A coastal table of poached Irish salmon\, dulse and ca
 rrageen pudding\, Bangor oysters\, brown soda bread with salted butter\, a
 nd a pot of tea or a measure of Bushmills.\nDay: Tuesday\n\nIcon: 🧜‍
 ♀️\nCategory: religious\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agen
 da/feast-of-st-muirgen-li-ban-the-mermaid/\nRecipes:\nPoached Irish Salmon
 : https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/poached-irish-salmon/\nDulse and 
 Carrageen Pudding: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/dulse-and-carrag
 een-pudding/\nBaked Bangor Oysters with Garlic Herb Butter: https://mss.ca
 stalia.institute/recipes/bangor-oysters/\nBrown Soda Bread with Salted But
 ter: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/brown-soda-bread-with-salted-b
 utter/\nClassic Brewed Black Tea: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/t
 ea/\nLí Ban's Seafoam Whiskey Cocktail: https://mss.castalia.institute/re
 cipes/bushmills-whiskey/
CATEGORIES:religious
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/st-muirgen-mermaid.svg
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/feast-of-st-muirgen-li-ban-the-mermaid/
END:VEVENT
