SUMMARY:Lunar New Year (Chunjie)
DESCRIPTION:History: Rooted in Han dynasty agrarian cycles\, the Lunar New 
 Year welcomes spring with family reunions\, ancestor veneration\, and hope
 s for prosperity.\nTraditions: Homes are scrubbed\, red lanterns strung\, 
 hongbao envelopes gifted\, and lion or dragon dances chase away lingering 
 Nian monsters.\nFeasting: Reunion banquets showcase longevity noodles\, wh
 ole fish\, dumplings shaped like ingots\, sweet rice cakes\, and mandarin 
 oranges for abundance.\nDay: Thursday\n\nIcon: 🐉\nCategory: cultural\n\
 nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/lunar-new-year-chunjie/\nRe
 cipes:\nLongevity Noodles with Pork and Vegetables: https://mss.castalia.i
 nstitute/recipes/longevity-noodles/\nSteamed Whole Fish for Lunar New Year
 : https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/whole-fish/\nChinese Pork and Cab
 bage Dumplings (Jiaozi): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/dumplings/
 \nSweet Lunar New Year Rice Cakes (Nian Gao): https://mss.castalia.institu
 te/recipes/sweet-rice-cakes/\nFestive Mandarin Orange Presentation: https:
 //mss.castalia.institute/recipes/mandarin-oranges/
CATEGORIES:cultural
