SUMMARY:Losar (Tibetan New Year)
DESCRIPTION:History: Losar blends ancient Bon winter rites with Buddhist ob
 servances\, dating to the era of King Trisong Detsen and now marking the T
 ibetan calendar's turning.\nTraditions: Families replace prayer flag strea
 mers\, visit monasteries for cham dances\, and exchange khata scarves whil
 e reciting auspicious wishes.\nFeasting: Households prepare guthuk noodle 
 soup with symbolic dumplings\, deep-fried khapse pastries\, dried yak chee
 se\, and butter tea shared with neighbours.\nDay: Thursday\n\nIcon: 🏔
 ️\nCategory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/l
 osar-tibetan-new-year/\nRecipes:\nGuthuk Noodle Soup: https://mss.castalia
 .institute/recipes/guthuk-noodle-soup/\nLosar Guthuk (Tibetan Symbolic Dum
 pling Soup): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/symbolic-dumplings/\nD
 eep-Fried Khapse Pastries: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/deep-fri
 ed-khapse-pastries/\nPrepared Dried Yak Cheese (Chhurpi): https://mss.cast
 alia.institute/recipes/dried-yak-cheese/\nTibetan Butter Tea (Po Cha): htt
 ps://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/butter-tea/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
