SUMMARY:Imbolc Eve (La Fheile Bride)
DESCRIPTION:History: Imbolc heralds the first stirrings of spring in ancien
 t Gaelic tradition\, bridged later with the veneration of Saint Brigid of 
 Kildare.\nTraditions: Families fashion Brigid's crosses\, set out corn dol
 lies to receive the saint's blessing\, and keep vigil fires burning throug
 h the night.\nFeasting: Dairy-rich dishes--fresh butter\, soft cheeses\, o
 atcakes\, and early lamb stews--honour Brigid's patronage of livestock and
  the hearth.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🌙\nCategory: seasonal\n\nAgenda: htt
 ps://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/imbolc-eve-la-fheile-bride/\nRecipes:\n
 Fresh Hand-Churned Imbolc Butter: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/f
 resh-butter/\nHerbed Fresh Goat Cheese Spread for Imbolc: https://mss.cast
 alia.institute/recipes/soft-cheeses/\nTraditional Scottish Oatcakes: https
 ://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/oatcakes/\nImbolc Eve Early Lamb Stew: h
 ttps://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/early-lamb-stews/
CATEGORIES:seasonal
