SUMMARY:Imbolc Day Celebration
DESCRIPTION:History: With the lambing season underway\, Imbolc marks the mi
 dpoint between solstice and equinox\, long tied to the rebirth of light an
 d Brigid's protective cloak.\nTraditions: Pilgrims visit holy wells\, spri
 nkle thresholds with blessed water\, and hang swaddles outdoors to absorb 
 Brigid's healing power.\nFeasting: Communities share bannocks\, colcannon\
 , dulse\, and honeyed porridges\, often concluding with tea infused with t
 he first tender herbs.\nDay: Sunday\n\nIcon: 🌱\nCategory: seasonal\n\nA
 genda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/imbolc-day-celebration/\nReci
 pes:\nTraditional Scottish Oat Bannocks: https://mss.castalia.institute/re
 cipes/bannocks/\nTraditional Colcannon: https://mss.castalia.institute/rec
 ipes/colcannon/\nToasted Dulse Crisps: https://mss.castalia.institute/reci
 pes/dulse/\nHoneyed Porridge: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/honey
 ed-porridge/\nImbolc Awakening Herbal Tea: https://mss.castalia.institute/
 recipes/herbal-tea/
