SUMMARY:Buddhist Ghost Festival (Ullambana)
DESCRIPTION:History: In many East and Southeast Asian Buddhist and folk tra
 ditions\, the Ghost Festival (Ullambana\, Zhongyuan) marks a time when off
 erings are made for ancestors and hungry ghosts.\nTraditions: Families vis
 it temples\, burn incense\, offer food\, and set out lanterns or paper off
 erings to guide and comfort wandering spirits.\nFeasting: Seasonal plates 
 vary by region\, often including rice\, fruit\, tea\, vegetarian dishes\, 
 and family recipes shared in remembrance.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🏮\nCate
 gory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/buddhist-g
