SUMMARY:St. Catherine's Day
DESCRIPTION:History: Medieval guilds honoured St. Catherine of Alexandria a
 s a patron of scholars and spinners\, with France's unmarried milliners be
 comi ng joyful "Catherinettes" on her November feast.\nTraditions: 🔮 Po
 uring wax  through an old key into cold water\, then reading the candlelit
  shadow—heart foretells love\, house promises stability\, animal hints a
 t a future spouse' s character\, ship signals travel—before whirling a b
 right St. Catherine's w heel procession through the streets.\nFeasting: Ba
 keries share saffron catter n cakes\, honeyed biscuits\, mulled cider\, an
 d spiced wine served after even ing vespers.\nDay: Tuesday\n\nIcon: 🎡\n
