 teamboat in the nineteenth century\, blending Saint Nicholas lore with mar
 itime identity.\nTraditions: On the first Saturday after Saint Martin's Da
 y Sinterklaas docks with his Pieten helpers\, parades through town distrib
 uting pepernoten\, and listens to children's wish lists before 5 December 
 gifts.\nFeasting: Crowds crunch spiced pepernoten\, speculaas windmill coo
 kies\, chocolate letters\,and marzipan while sipping hot cocoa along the c
 anals.\nDay: Saturday\n\nIcon: 🚢\nCategory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https:/
