SUMMARY:Feast of Our Lady of Guadalupe
DESCRIPTION:History: In 1531 Juan Diego reported Marian apparitions on Tepe
 yac Hill\, and the tilma image quickly became a symbol of Mexican faith an
 d identity.\nTraditions: Pilgrims serenade the Virgin with mananitas\, off
 er roses at the basilica\, and reenact the miracle in parish plazas across
  the Americas.\nFeasting: Peregrinos se reponen con tamales verdes\, tamal
 es de rajas con queso\, pozole rojo\, mole poblano con arroz\, tacos dorad
 os\, bunuelos de viento\, churros de canela\, champurrado espumoso\, y ato
 le de guayaba antes de continuar las serenatas.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🌹
