SUMMARY:St. Lucia's Day
DESCRIPTION:History: Modern Lucia celebrations took shape in early twentiet
 h-century Sweden\, transforming a regional custom into a nationwide festiv
 al of light in darkness.\nTraditions: Girls and boys form Lucia trains in 
 schools and workplaces\, delivering songs and saffron buns to symbolise ho
 pe during the polar night.\nFeasting: Households share lussekatter\, saffr
 on biscotti\, almond cookies\, and glasses of julmust or coffee to accompa
 ny the morning serenade.\nDay: Saturday\n\nIcon: 🕯️\nCategory: cultur
 al\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/st-lucias-day/\nRecipe
