SUMMARY:Gaudete Sunday
DESCRIPTION:History: Named for the "Gaudete in Domino" introit\, the third 
 Advent Sunday relaxes penitential tones with joyful anticipation noted sin
 ce the Middle Ages.\nTraditions: Churches light the rose candle\, priests 
 wear rose vestments\, and choirs sing jubilant hymns heralding the nearnes
 s of Christmas.\nFeasting: In the Philippines\, Simbang Gabi worshippers e
 njoy bibingka and puto bumbong\, while others serve rosy macarons and warm
  fruit punch.\nDay: Sunday\n\nIcon: 🕯️\nCategory: cultural\n\nAgenda:
  https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/gaudete-sunday/\nRecipes:\nBibingka
  (Traditional Filipino Baked Rice Cake): https://mss.castalia.institute/re
 cipes/bibingka/\nPuto Bumbong: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/puto
 -bumbong/\nRose Raspberry Macarons for Gaudete Sunday: https://mss.castali
 a.institute/recipes/macarons/\nGaudete Sunday Festive Fruit Punch: https:/
 /mss.castalia.institute/recipes/fruit-punch/
CATEGORIES:cultural
