SUMMARY:Hanukkah (Festival of Lights)
DESCRIPTION:History: Hanukkah commemorates the Maccabean rededication of th
 e Temple in 164 BCE and the rabbinic tale of oil that miraculously lasted 
 eight nights.\nTraditions: Families kindle the menorah\, recite blessings\
 , play dreidel games\, give gelt\, and emphasise acts of charity and resil
 ience.\nFeasting: Foods fried in oil--potato latkes\, sufganiyot\, bimuelo
 s--and braised brisket or kugel anchor the festive tables.\nDay: Monday\n\
 nIcon: 🕎\nCategory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/
