SUMMARY:Saturnalia
DESCRIPTION:History: Rome's Saturnalia\, attested as early as 217 BCE\, hon
 oured Saturn with a public holiday of role reversal\, gift giving\, and te
 mporary liberty for enslaved people.\nTraditions: Participants shout "Io S
 aturnalia!"\, wear felt pileus caps\, and elect mock kings who preside ove
 r games and generous exchanges.\nFeasting: Banquets overflow with roast po
 rk\, olives\, mulsum sweet wine\, pine nuts\, and honey cakes shared betwe
 en patrons and dependents.\nDay: Wednesday\n\nIcon: 🏛️\nCategory: cul
 tural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/saturnalia/\nRecipe
 s:\nSaturnalia Roast Pork: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/roast-po
 rk/\nMarinated Olives for Saturnalia: https://mss.castalia.institute/recip
 es/olives/\nMulsum Sweet Wine: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/muls
 um-sweet-wine/\nHoney-Glazed Pine Nuts for Saturnalia: https://mss.castali
 a.institute/recipes/pine-nuts/\nSaturnalia Honey Cakes: https://mss.castal
 ia.institute/recipes/honey-cakes/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
