SUMMARY:Polaris Meteor Watch & UFO Evening
DESCRIPTION:History: Stargazers gather during the solstice week to trace me
 teor showers as they skim past Polaris, blending folk UFO lore with real n
 ight-sky science.\nTraditions: Neighbors hang neon saucer lanterns, align 
 telescopes north, lead children in meteor-counting logs, and play synth ca
 rols while a laser pointer traces the Little Dipper.\nFeasting: Camps pour
  midnight cocoa tinted nebula-blue, share smoky chili, citrus-rosemary pop
 corn, and shortbread saucers dusted with edible stardust.\nDay: Monday\n\n
