DTSTAMP:20251104T055848Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20261220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20271220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20281220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20291220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20301220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20311220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20321220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20331220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20341220
RDATE;VALUE=DATE:20351220
X-MSS-DATE-SOURCE:https://calendar.ut.ac.ir/
X-MSS-PERSIAN-POLICY:University of Tehran Calendar Center Solar Hijri dates; Nowruz=1 Farvardin; Yalda=30 Azar
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251221
SUMMARY:Yalda Night
DESCRIPTION:History: Persian Yalda predates Islam\, celebrating the birth o
 f Mithra and later the victory of light over darkness on the longest night
 .\nTraditions: Families stay awake reading Hafez poetry\, storytelling\, a
 nd watching the fire's glow until the first light of dawn.\nFeasting: Aper
 itif glasses of sharbat-e anar o gol-e sorkh—pomegranate and rosewater c
 ordial with mint and lime—open the sofreh before meze of sabzi khordan w
 ith herbs\, feta\, walnuts\, and warm flatbread\, borani laboo beet yogurt
  with pistachio\, and zeytoon parvardeh olives in pomegranate molasses. Th
 e main spread features fesenjān of duck or chicken simmered to a glossy w
 alnut-pomegranate sauce\, tahchin-e zereshk saffron rice cake layered with
  barberries and tender chicken\, and khoresht-e bamieh okra stew for veget
 arians. Salad-e Shirazi and sesame-topped naan-e barbari brighten the tabl
 e\, while desserts showcase anar o hendevaneh fruit\, ajil-e Shab-e Yalda 
 roasted nuts and dried fruits for good fortune\, and sholeh zard saffron r
 ice pudding dusted with cinnamon. Guests close the vigil by drawing Hafez 
 divinations as poetry and the promise of returning light fill the night.\n
 Day: Saturday\n\nIcon: 🌙\nCategory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.cas
 talia.institute/agenda/yalda-night/\nRecipes:\nPomegranate and Rosewater C
 ordial: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/pomegranate-and-rosewater-c
 ordial/\nFresh Herb Platter with Feta and Walnuts: https://mss.castalia.in
 stitute/recipes/fresh-herb-platter-with-feta-and-walnuts/\nBeet Yogurt Dip
  with Pistachio: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/beet-yogurt-dip-wi
 th-pistachio/\nMarinated Olives with Pomegranate and Walnuts: https://mss.
 castalia.institute/recipes/marinated-olives-with-pomegranate-and-walnuts/\
 nFesenjan (Persian Walnut and Pomegranate Stew): https://mss.castalia.inst
 itute/recipes/walnut-pomegranate-stew-fesenjan/\nSaffron Rice Cake with Ba
 rberries and Chicken (Tahchin): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/saf
 fron-rice-cake-with-barberries-and-chicken-tahchin/\nOkra Stew (Khoresht-e
  Bamieh): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/okra-stew-khoresht-e-bami
 eh/\nShirazi Salad: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/shirazi-salad/\
 nBarbari Bread: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/barbari-bread/\nPom
 egranate and Watermelon Platter for Yalda Night: https://mss.castalia.inst
 itute/recipes/pomegranate-and-watermelon/\nYalda Night Ajeel (Mixed Nuts a
 nd Dried Fruits): https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/yalda-night-mixed
