UID:la-noche-de-rabanos@maybesomethingseasonal.com
DTSTAMP:20251104T055848Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251223
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251224
SUMMARY:La Noche de Rabanos
DESCRIPTION:History: Oaxaca's Night of the Radishes began in 1897 when farm
 ers carved oversized radishes to entice holiday shoppers\, becoming an off
 icial civic festival.\nTraditions: Artisans sculpt Nativity scenes\, dance
 rs\, and mythical beasts from radishes\, competing for prizes as bands and
  crowds stroll the zocalo.\nFeasting: Cena Tradicional Oaxaquena de Invier
 no features an ensalada de rabanos with lime and cilantro\, tamales de rab
 ano with bright raw radish salsa and atole verde de epazote\, champurrado 
 espeso de cacao y masa\, optional tamales dulces de pina y pasas\, and sip
 s of mezcal artesanal served with orange slices and sal de gusano.\nDay: T
 uesday\n\nIcon: 🥕\nCategory: cultural\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.i
 nstitute/agenda/la-noche-de-rabanos/\nRecipes:\nOaxacan Radish and Lime Sa
 lad: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/radish-salad/\nRadish and Ques
 illo Tamales: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/radish-tamales/\nEpaz
 ote Green Atole: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/epazote-green-atol
 e/\nThick Cocoa and Masa Champurrado: https://mss.castalia.institute/recip
 es/thick-cocoa-and-masa-champurrado/\nSweet Pineapple and Raisin Tamales: 
 https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/sweet-pineapple-and-raisin-tamales/
 \nTraditional Mezcal Service for La Noche de Rábanos: https://mss.castali
 a.institute/recipes/artisanal-mezcal/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/night-of-the-radishes-traditional-oaxacan-festival.png
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/la-noche-de-rabanos/
END:VEVENT
