UID:christmas-eve@maybesomethingseasonal.com
DTSTAMP:20251104T055848Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251224
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251225
SUMMARY:Christmas Eve
DESCRIPTION:History: Christian communities have kept the Nativity vigil sin
 ce the fourth century\, preparing through liturgies of lessons\, carols\, 
 and midnight Mass.\nTraditions: Families light Advent candles\, attend ser
 vices\, exchange modest gifts\, and observe the tradition of refraining fr
 om meat until the feast begins.\nFeasting: Italian Seven Fishes dinners\, 
 Polish wigilia with beet soup and pierogi\, and hot cocoa with cookies set
  the stage for the midnight celebration.\nDay: Wednesday\n\nIcon: 🌟\nCa
 tegory: religious\n\nAgenda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/christm
 as-eve/\nRecipes:\nSeafood Linguine for the Feast of the Seven Fishes: htt
 ps://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/feast-of-the-seven-fishes/\nChristmas 
 Eve Clear Beet Soup (Barszcz Wigilijny): https://mss.castalia.institute/re
 cipes/beet-soup/\nClassic Potato and Cheese Pierogi: https://mss.castalia.
 institute/recipes/pierogi/\nClassic Holiday Hot Cocoa: https://mss.castali
 a.institute/recipes/hot-cocoa/\nClassic Christmas Eve Sugar Cookies: https
 ://mss.castalia.institute/recipes/cookies/
CATEGORIES:religious
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/caga-tio.svg
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/christmas-eve/
END:VEVENT
