UID:st-stephen-s-day-boxing-day@maybesomethingseasonal.com
DTSTAMP:20251104T055848Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251226
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251227
SUMMARY:St. Stephen's Day (Boxing Day)
DESCRIPTION:History: St. Stephen\, the first Christian martyr\, is honoured
  on 26 December\; in Britain and Ireland the date also became Boxing Day f
 or giving to servants and the poor.\nTraditions: Foxhunts\, charity drives
 \, and visits to friends are common\, while in Ireland the Wren Boys once 
 paraded door to door collecting donations.\nFeasting: Leftover Christmas r
 oasts become hearty pies\, paired with bubble-and-squeak\, mince pies\, an
 d mugs of spiced ale.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: ⛪\nCategory: cultural\n\nAge
 nda: https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/st-stephens-day-boxing-day/\nRe
 cipes:\nHearty Steak and Mushroom Pie: https://mss.castalia.institute/reci
 pes/hearty-pie/\nBubble and Squeak: https://mss.castalia.institute/recipes
 /bubble-and-squeak/\nTraditional Mince Pies: https://mss.castalia.institut
 e/recipes/mince-pie/\nSpiced Ale (Wassail): https://mss.castalia.institute
 /recipes/spiced-ale/
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:/images/stefans-feast-stone.png
URL:https://mss.castalia.institute/agenda/st-stephens-day-boxing-day/
